No, this feature would require a source generator.
The following extension method could be used to ensure the RPC name is correct, but the argument types cannot be checked at compile time:
```cs
public static void Rpc(this Action action, params Variant[] args)
{
	((Node)action.Target).Rpc(action.Method.Name, args);
}

// Can be run like this:
((Action)Jump).Rpc(foo,bar)
```
